# Tomato Tortilla Soup

Status: Untested

## Recipe Name:
Tomato Tortilla Soup

## Servings:
6

## Prep Time:
10 minutes

## Cook Time:
20 minutes

## Ingredients:
### Soup
- 1 tablespoon olive oil
- 1 small onion, chopped
- 3 cloves garlic, finely minced
- 1 small jalapeño, seeded and finely chopped
- 1 teaspoon ground cumin
- 3/4 teaspoon dried oregano
- 4 cups low-sodium chicken or vegetable stock
- 2 cans (14.5 ounces each) no-salt-added diced tomatoes with juice
- 1/4 cup fresh lime juice
- 1/4 teaspoon kosher salt, or to taste

### Tortilla Strips
- 2 corn tortillas, 6-inch
- 1 teaspoon olive oil
- Kosher salt, for sprinkling

### Garnishes
- 1/4 cup reduced-fat sour cream
- 2 tablespoons fresh cilantro leaves, chopped

## Instructions:
1. Heat 1 tablespoon olive oil in a large heavy skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and cook, stirring often, for 5 minutes, until soft and translucent.
2. Add the garlic, jalapeño, cumin, and oregano. Cook for 1 minute more.
3. Add the stock and tomatoes. Bring to a boil, then reduce the heat to low and simmer for 10 minutes.
4. Heat the oven to 375 F. Brush both sides of the tortillas lightly with the remaining 1 teaspoon olive oil. Cut the tortillas into strips about 1/4 inch wide.
5. Arrange the strips on a foil-lined baking sheet. Sprinkle them lightly with kosher salt. Bake for about 12 minutes, until crisp and golden. Remove and cool.
6. Remove the soup from the heat. Stir in the lime juice. Taste and add salt if needed.
7. Blend the soup partially with an immersion blender, leaving some chunky tomato pieces.
8. Serve topped with the tortilla strips, sour cream, and cilantro.

Use vegetable stock for a vegetarian version. Leave the soup partly chunky; a fully smooth puree loses the body that makes this soup work.

Source: Sharon Rigsby, "Tomato Tortilla Soup - A Quick and Easy Recipe". Grits and Pinecones. https://www.gritsandpinecones.com/tomato-tortilla-soup/

